 There are 10 miles that Rosie runs in an hour for 3 hours. So,



$$\begin{align}

10&\times 3 \\

&=30

\end{align}

$$



There are 5 miles that Rosie runs in an hour for the remaining 4 hours (7  – 3 = 4) in an hour. So,



$$\begin{align}

5&\times 4\\

&=20

\end{align}

$$



Hence she can run 30 miles in an hour for 3 hours and 20 miles in an hour for 4 hours. So,



$$\begin{align}

30+20=50

\end{align}

$$



She can run 50 miles in 7 hours.
